+<a id="deepseek-aidsh-tool-plan-mode"></a>
+
+## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-plan-mode`
+
+### `enter_plan_mode`
+
+Propose switching this session into plan mode. Use it before starting non-trivial implementation work when the user should approve the approach first. In plan mode you research and plan; implementation waits until your exit_plan_mode call is approved. The switch applies from your next step; the user can cancel it or leave plan mode at any time with /plan off.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {}
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/plan/tool-plan-mode/src/index.ts`](../packages/plan/tool-plan-mode/src/index.ts)
+
+### `exit_plan_mode`
+
+Use only in plan mode. Present your plan for the user's review and, on approval, leave plan mode. Send the COMPLETE plan as markdown, starting with a # heading that names it. The user may approve (carry out the plan from your next step) or keep planning — their feedback comes back in the tool result; revise and present again.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "plan": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "The complete plan, as markdown, starting with a # heading that names it."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "plan"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/plan/tool-plan-mode/src/index.ts`](../packages/plan/tool-plan-mode/src/index.ts)
+
+enter_plan_mode forwards the model's intent to the plan-mode controller; an in-turn call queues the switch for the next accepted pre-step, and leaving plan mode stays gated by exit_plan_mode's user review.
+
+<a id="deepseek-aidsh-automations"></a>
+
+## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-automations`
+
+### `automation_cancel`
+
+Cancel one scheduled automation by id. Idempotent per id: cancelling an unknown id reports so.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "id": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "The automation id from automation_create or automation_list."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "id"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts`](../packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts)
+
+### `automation_create`
+
+Schedule a recurring or one-shot automation: store a prompt that spawns a FRESH session in this workspace when due. The process must be running at the due time; missed occurrences coalesce into one catch-up fire.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "title": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "A short (3-5 word) label shown in list output and as the spawned session title."
+    },
+    "prompt": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "The complete, self-contained task the spawned session will receive as its user message. It starts with no context from this conversation."
+    },
+    "kind": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "\"after\" fires once delay_seconds from now; \"at\" fires once at the ISO-8601 `at` timestamp; \"every\" fires on a fixed rate of interval_seconds. \"after\" and \"at\" are one-shot."
+    },
+    "delay_seconds": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Seconds from now until the one-shot fire (kind \"after\")."
+    },
+    "at": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "ISO-8601 timestamp of the one-shot fire (kind \"at\")."
+    },
+    "interval_seconds": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Fixed-rate interval in seconds (kind \"every\")."
+    },
+    "max_runs": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Fire ceiling for recurring (\"every\") automations; omit for unbounded."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "title",
+    "prompt",
+    "kind"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts`](../packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts)
+
+### `automation_list`
+
+List the scheduled automations of this deployment with their next fire times.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {}
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts`](../packages/schedule/automations/src/index.ts)
+
+The three bounds are required deployment config; the shipped base bundle carries 65536/60/60. Firing spawns a fresh session through `ctx.agents.create` and touches no session log, and spawn-time services (`agents`, `agentPresets`) resolve at fire time.
+
